Use IBM Plex Sans for the interface on Windows

The Windows counterpart of patches/0004: menus, tabs, toolbars and Settings
use IBM Plex Sans at the size and weight Windows asks for. Form controls keep
the native font so web pages render as in Firefox.

diff --git a/widget/windows/nsLookAndFeel.cpp b/widget/windows/nsLookAndFeel.cpp
index f63dd0f..8dd577a 100644
--- a/widget/windows/nsLookAndFeel.cpp
+++ b/widget/windows/nsLookAndFeel.cpp
@@ -862,6 +862,15 @@ LookAndFeelFont nsLookAndFeel::GetLookAndFeelFont(LookAndFeel::FontID anID) {
 bool nsLookAndFeel::NativeGetFont(LookAndFeel::FontID anID, nsString& aFontName,
                                   gfxFontStyle& aFontStyle) {
   LookAndFeelFont font = GetLookAndFeelFont(anID);
+  // Hallow: the interface font is IBM Plex Sans (bundled in <app>/fonts), at
+  // the size and weight Windows asks for, as on Linux. Form-control fonts
+  // (fields, lists, buttons) stay native so web pages render as they do in
+  // Firefox. The ui.font.* prefs can still pick a different font.
+  if (font.haveFont() && anID != LookAndFeel::FontID::MozField &&
+      anID != LookAndFeel::FontID::MozList &&
+      anID != LookAndFeel::FontID::MozButton) {
+    font.name() = u"IBM Plex Sans"_ns;
+  }
   return LookAndFeelFontToStyle(font, aFontName, aFontStyle);
 }
 
